Accept only "inf" and "infinity" as an infinite sleep.
sleep compared just the first three characters of its first argument
with "inf", so any argument that began with them, such as "information"
or "infinity5", made it sleep forever instead of failing as an invalid
number. Compare the whole argument, ignoring case, for the spellings
the comment says GNU sleep accepts.

---
 coreutils/sleep.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/coreutils/sleep.c
+++ b/coreutils/sleep.c
@@ -84,7 +84,9 @@
 	}
 
 	/* GNU sleep accepts "inf", "INF", "infinity" and "INFINITY" */
-	if (strncasecmp(argv[0], "inf", 3) == 0)
+	if (strcasecmp(argv[0], "inf") == 0
+	 || strcasecmp(argv[0], "infinity") == 0
+	)
 		for (;;)
 			sleep(INT_MAX);
 
